    "mode": "tts_only"
  },
  "transcript": [
    {
      "t": 2.54,
      "text": "This is a simple example where we want",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 5.74,
      "text": "to just apply the formula for conditional probabilities",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 8.16,
      "text": "and see what we get.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 10.44,
      "text": "The example involves a four-sided die, if",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 14.76,
      "text": "you can imagine such an object, which we",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 17.32,
      "text": "roll twice and we record the first roll",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 19.98,
      "text": "and the second roll, so there are 16",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 22.54,
      "text": "possible outcomes.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 23.62,
      "text": "We assume to keep things simple that each",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 27.66,
      "text": "one of those 16 possible outcomes, each one",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 31.68,
      "text": "of them has the same probability, so each",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 33.98,
      "text": "outcome has probability 1 over 16.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 39.32,
      "text": "Let us consider now a particular event B",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 42.64,
      "text": "on which we are going to condition.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 44.42,
      "text": "This is the event under which the smaller",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 47.96,
      "text": "of the two die rolls is equal to",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 50.66,
      "text": "2, which means that one of the dies",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 53.7,
      "text": "must have resulted in 2, and the other",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 56.5,
      "text": "die has resulted in something which is 2",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 59.72,
      "text": "or larger.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 60.4,
      "text": "So this can happen in multiple ways, and",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 64.1,
      "text": "here are the different ways that it can",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 66.6,
      "text": "happen.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 67.24,
      "text": "So a 2, 2, or a 2, 3,",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 69.38,
      "text": "a 2, 4, then a 3, 2, and",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 73.22,
      "text": "a 4, 2, all these are outcomes in",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 75.74,
      "text": "which one of the dies has a value",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 78.38,
      "text": "equal to 2, and the other die is",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 80.34,
      "text": "at least as large.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 82.22,
      "text": "So we condition on this event.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 85.02,
      "text": "These results in a conditional model where each",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 88.58,
      "text": "one of those five outcomes are equally likely",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 92.06,
      "text": "since they used to be equally likely in",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 94.82,
      "text": "the original model.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 96.56,
      "text": "Now let us look at this quantity, the",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 98.76,
      "text": "maximum of the two die rolls, that is",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 101.62,
      "text": "the largest of the results, and let us",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 104.5,
      "text": "try to calculate the following quantity, the conditional",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 108.26,
      "text": "probability that the maximum is equal to 1",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 111.22,
      "text": "given that the minimum is equal to 2.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 114.52,
      "text": "So this is the conditional probability of this",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 118.1,
      "text": "particular outcome.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 119.82,
      "text": "While this particular outcome cannot happen, if I",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 122.72,
      "text": "tell you that the smaller number is 2,",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 125.38,
      "text": "then the larger number cannot be equal to",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 128.18,
      "text": "1.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 128.82,
      "text": "So this outcome is impossible, and therefore this",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 131.32,
      "text": "conditional probability is equal to 0.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 134.6,
      "text": "Let's do something a little more interesting.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 136.72,
      "text": "Let us now look at the conditional probability",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 139.52,
      "text": "that the maximum is equal to 3 given",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 144.66,
      "text": "the information that event B has occurred.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 149.14,
      "text": "It's best to draw a picture and see",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 150.9,
      "text": "what that event corresponds to.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 153.86,
      "text": "M is equal to 3, the maximum is",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 156.56,
      "text": "equal to 3, if 1 of the dies",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 161.06,
      "text": "resulted in a 3, and the other die",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 164.28,
      "text": "resulting in something that's 3 or less.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 168.32,
      "text": "So this event here corresponds to the blue",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 173.56,
      "text": "region in this diagram.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 176.26,
      "text": "Now let us try to calculate the conditional",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 179.4,
      "text": "probability by just following the definition.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 182.76,
      "text": "The conditional probability of one event given another",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 186.88,
      "text": "is the probability that both of them, both",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 191.06,
      "text": "of the two events occur divided by the",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 197.5,
      "text": "probability of the conditioning event.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 199.88,
      "text": "That is, out of the total probability in",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 203.74,
      "text": "the conditioning event, we ask what fraction of",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 206.76,
      "text": "that probability is assigned to outcomes in which",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 210.02,
      "text": "the event of interest is also happening.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 213.96,
      "text": "So what is this event?",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 216.18,
      "text": "The maximum is equal to 3, which is",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 218.4,
      "text": "the blue event, and simultaneously the red event",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 222.96,
      "text": "is happening.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 223.74,
      "text": "These two events intersect only in two places.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 228.68,
      "text": "This is the intersection of the two events,",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 231.3,
      "text": "and the probability of that intersection is 2",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 236.12,
      "text": "out of 16.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 238.18,
      "text": "Since there's 16 outcomes, and that event happens",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 241.18,
      "text": "only with two particular outcomes.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 244.82,
      "text": "So this gives us 2 over 16 in",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 247.4,
      "text": "the numerator.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 249.22,
      "text": "How about the denominator?",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 251.28,
      "text": "Event B consists of a total of 5",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 253.78,
      "text": "possible outcomes, which one has probability 1 16,",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 257.26,
      "text": "so this is 5 over 16, so the",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 259.94,
      "text": "final answer is 2 over 5.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 263.42,
      "text": "We could have gotten that same answer in",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 266.04,
      "text": "a simple and perhaps more intuitive way.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 269.8,
      "text": "In the original model, all outcomes were equally",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 272.34,
      "text": "likely.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 273.58,
      "text": "Therefore, in the conditional model, the five outcomes",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 277.1,
      "text": "that belong to B should also be equally",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 280.06,
      "text": "likely.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 281.14,
      "text": "Out of those five, there's two of them",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 283.58,
      "text": "that make the event of interest to occur,",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 288.14,
      "text": "so given that we live in B, there's",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 290.92,
      "text": "two ways out of five that the event",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 293.02,
      "text": "of interest will materialize, so the event of",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 295.8,
      "text": "interest has conditional probability equals to two-fifths.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    }
  ],
